9. ANIMATION IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS

9.1 Deterministic timing

All animations must be repeatable.

Use a centralized timeline configuration. Each scene must define:

- Start time.
- End time.
- Frame count.
- UI animation timing.
- Camera animation timing.
- Audio start/end.
- Transition duration.
- Required assets.

Do not rely on random animation delays or manual interactive actions during rendering.

9.2 Reusable UI components

Implement reusable components for:

- Chat bubbles.
- Typing indicators.
- Information extraction cards.
- Currency parsing pipeline.
- Lead score badges.
- Notification cards.
- CRM lists.
- Review status.
- Property cards.
- Search filters.
- Booking calendar.
- Invoice preview.
- PWA installation prompt.

Use shared design tokens for colors, typography, spacing, shadows and motion.

9.3 Text rendering

- Render all important UI text as real text, not generated image lettering.
- Use local fonts to prevent missing-font failures.
- Maintain readable text sizes at 4K.
- Avoid excessive text density.
- Keep subtitles inside safe margins.
- Verify Hindi-English spelling.

10. 4K RENDERING PIPELINE

Implement a resumable rendering pipeline.

Step 1: Validate installed dependencies.

Step 2: Validate all required assets and configuration.

Step 3: Generate UI animation frames.

Step 4: Render Blender scenes.

Step 5: Composite UI and 3D layers.

Step 6: Generate and validate narration timing.

Step 7: Mix music and sound effects.

Step 8: Add subtitles.

Step 9: Assemble scenes with transitions.

Step 10: Export the final 4K MP4.

Step 11: Inspect the output with ffprobe.

Step 12: Generate a production report.

Use frame sequences to support render recovery. Do not delete successful renders when another scene fails.

Do not rerender unchanged scenes unless necessary.

